# Firebase Ranking 1.0 Phase 1A (Issue #87) -- Firebase Web app config.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (already gitignored via the repo's `*.local` pattern) and
# fill in real values from the Firebase Console (Project settings -> General -> Your apps ->
# Web app -> SDK setup and configuration -> Config). See
# docs/design/TETO_FIREBASE-RANKING_SETUP.md for the full manual setup walkthrough.
#
# A Firebase Web `apiKey` is NOT a secret -- it only identifies which Firebase project a
# request targets; access is enforced by Firestore/Storage security rules (and, in a later
# phase, App Check), not by hiding this value. It is safe to expose in a public client bundle.
#
# Never put a service account / Admin SDK private key here or anywhere in this repo -- those
# belong only in a trusted server environment (a future Cloud Functions deployment's own
# config), never in a GitHub Pages client build.
#
# All four vars below are required together. Leaving any of them unset (e.g. an untouched
# `.env.local`, or CI/local dev with no Firebase project yet) makes the app treat Firebase as
# fully unconfigured -- offline gameplay (HOME/FREE/Lunch Rush/Shop/Dex/Inventory) is
# unaffected either way.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
